.TH LIBEASYMCP2221 3 "July 2026" "libeasymcp2221" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
libeasymcp2221 \- C library for MCP2221 USB-to-I2C/GPIO bridges

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libeasymcp2221/mcp2221.h>
.B #include <libeasymcp2221/constants.h>

.BI "mcp2221_t *mcp2221_open_simple(uint16_t " vid ", uint16_t " pid ", int " devnum ","
.BI "                                  const char *" usbserial ", int " i2c_speed_hz ");"
.BI "void mcp2221_close(mcp2221_t *" dev ");"
.fi

Link with:
.BR "pkg-config --cflags --libs libeasymcp2221"

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B libeasymcp2221
library is a C port of the EasyMCP2221 Python module for Microchip
MCP2221/MCP2221A USB-to-I2C/GPIO bridge chips. It exposes a C-style API with
explicit device handles and
.B mcp_err_t
return values instead of Python classes and exceptions.

Key capabilities include:
.IP \[bu] 2
Opening and closing MCP2221 devices by VID/PID, index or USB serial.
.IP \[bu] 2
I2C master read/write operations with explicit transfer kinds and timeouts.
.IP \[bu] 2
SMBus and I2C-slave convenience helpers.
.IP \[bu] 2
GPIO read/write, GPIO polling and pin-function configuration.
.IP \[bu] 2
ADC, DAC, clock, IOC, SRAM and flash settings helpers.

.SH API NAMING
Preferred public API names use the
.B mcp2221_*
function prefix,
.B mcp2221_*_t
type names and
.B MCP2221_*
macro names. Legacy names remain available as compatibility aliases for the
1.x series and may be removed in a future major release.

Define
.B MCP2221_NO_DEPRECATED_WARNINGS
before including libeasymcp2221 headers to suppress compatibility warnings
while migrating old code.

.SH RETURN VALUES
Most functions return
.B MCP_ERR_OK
on success or another
.B mcp_err_t
value on failure. Functions that return payload lengths use output parameters.
Use
.B mcp_error_code_to_string()
to convert error codes to symbolic strings.

.SH RESOURCE OWNERSHIP
Handles returned by
.B mcp2221_open*()
are owned by the caller and must be released with
.BR mcp2221_close() .

.B mcp2221_smbus_init()
borrows an existing MCP2221 handle when one is supplied. Otherwise it opens its
own handle, which is released by
.BR mcp2221_smbus_close() .

.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <libeasymcp2221/mcp2221.h>
#include <libeasymcp2221/constants.h>

int main(void) {
    mcp2221_t *dev = mcp2221_open_simple(MCP2221_DEV_DEFAULT_VID,
                                          MCP2221_DEV_DEFAULT_PID,
                                          0, NULL, 100000);
    if (!dev)
        return 1;

    mcp_err_t err = mcp2221_i2c_set_speed(dev, 100000);
    mcp2221_close(dev);

    return err == MCP_ERR_OK ? 0 : 1;
}
.fi

